  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining App Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the app\'s architecture and essential features to flawlessly meet user needs. I\'ve begun detailing the database design, specifically the `WorkoutLog` entity using Room. I\'m aiming for a robust and efficient structure to manage workout data effectively.\n\n\n**Detailing Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the specific data structures. Now, I\'m defining the database entities in detail. I\'ve outlined the fields for `WorkoutLog`, including exercise specifics like `exerciseName`, `muscleGroup`, reps, weight, and even RPE and raw voice input. I\'m also specifying data types for everything, like `date` as a string and timestamp as a long. After WorkoutLog, I\'ve started defining the `DietLog` entity as well.\n\n\n**Defining User Profile**\n\nI\'m now detailing the `UserProfile` entity, planning to integrate it with DataStore and Room for robust storage. I\'m solidifying attributes like weight, height, age, gender, activity level, and target calorie deficit. I\'ve also added goal type options for broader user targeting. The attributes are being fleshed out, including setting default values for typical user configurations.\n\n\n**Developing AI Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into AI features. I\'m focusing on two key aspects: a nutrition analyzer and a progressive overload advisor. The nutrition analyzer will estimate calories and macronutrients from food descriptions, even handling offline scenarios. The progressive overload advisor analyzes workout history to suggest precise weight increments or rep/set adjustments. This should help users optimize their progress effectively.\n\n\n**Implementing AI Diagnostic**\n\nI\'m now integrating an AI overload diagnostic using Gemini, which analyzes a user\'s workout trends for personalized recommendations. Additionally, I am developing a speech & dictation module with Android\'s `SpeechRecognizer` and a floating voice dictation interface with waveform animation. I\'m also preparing pre-set prompts for quick voice entry of workout and diet data with AI extraction.\n\n\n**Visualizing Data Progress**\n\nI\'m now focusing on data visualization for the UI. I\'m working on a progress meter to show the current vs. target calorie deficit, including visual indicators like a gauge and arc with detailed values. Additionally, I\'m designing a macronutrient balance bar. I\'m also planning history and analytics features to review progress by week, month, or year. I\'m adding timeframe selection and interactive charts.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 350080876
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
