    thinking: "**Analyzing User Needs**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving deep into the specifics of the user\'s request. My focus right now is on directly addressing the voice logging and the gram-accurate caloric calculation components. I\'m breaking down the features into smaller, manageable chunks to ensure each piece fits seamlessly together. Considering the dual goals, I must prioritize ease of voice input and calculation accuracy.\n\n\n**Refining Parsing Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the voice input parsing within `GeminiFitnessService.kt`. The system prompt in `parseDietVoice` is being enhanced to precisely extract food items and quantities, like \"\351\270\241\350\203\270\350\202\211 200g\". Simultaneously, I\'m constructing a robust food database parser in `fallbackParseDiet` to handle various quantity formats and provide accurate nutritional breakdowns per item, including calories, protein, carbs, and fat, ensuring precise calculation of total meal calories. I plan to display this information in the `DietConfirmationDialog` next.\n\n\n**Enhancing Data Display**\n\nI\'m focusing on user interface improvements now. Specifically, I\'m working to display extracted food items with their gram weights and calories in real-time, giving users the ability to adjust or remove items and see the total meal calories updated instantly! In `DietScreen.kt`, I\'m developing a clear display for daily and meal caloric content, integrating voice and manual logging, and adding a dynamic deficit progress bar across the diet screen and dashboard for better tracking. Further, the deficit gauge card and dashboard will feature interactive visual indicators, a deficit ring and progress bar.\n\n\n"
