  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Diet Display**\n\nI\'m working on improving the `DietConfirmationDialog`\'s presentation. My current focus is to display a breakdown of each food item, including estimated gram amounts and their approximate caloric values, which is much more informative than just listing names. I\'m aiming for a clear and concise format like, \"\351\246\231\347\205\216\351\270\241\350\203\270\350\202\211 (200g) - 266 kcal\". This breakdown would provide users with a more detailed understanding of their dietary intake.\n\n\n**Enhancing Input and Parsing**\n\nI\'ve significantly updated how I handle voice input to be more versatile and precise. My focus is on refining the system prompt and fallback parsing in `GeminiFitnessService.kt` to handle various measurements like grams, milliliters, and counts (\"200\345\205\213\", \"200g\", \"2\344\270\252\351\270\241\350\233\213\"). I\'m also ensuring the calorie calculation is accurate, using standard nutrition data for items like chicken, beef, pork, and eggs. The diet display now features editable item quantities, with a real-time recalculation of the total caloric content. A clear display of the voice input text, with a prominent total calories display, and macronutrient breakdown is added.\n\n\n**Calculating Calorie Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed calorie information for common foods. I\'ve compiled values for items like rice, oats, bread, milk, whey, vegetables, and various fruits, nuts, and proteins. I\'m focusing on providing estimated caloric values per gram and total macronutrient breakdowns (protein, carbs, and fats). I\'m structuring this data for easy integration into the diet display.\n\n\n"
